<speak>
<s>From <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news, this is your briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">24032026</say-as>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="95%">
<s>Pakistani jets struck a rehabilitation center in Kabul during Ramadan iftar, killing at least four hundred patients — families' last resort in a country where public healthcare has all but collapsed.</s> <s>The facility held up to eighteen hundred people, many sent by relatives with nowhere else to turn.</s> <s>The Taliban has vowed retaliation, and family members are still digging through the wreckage searching for the missing.</s>
</prosody>
<p>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>A Sudanese military drone struck a funeral in Chad, killing fifteen mourners who'd crossed the border seeking safety.</s> <s>The Rapid Support Forces retook the town of Bara for the second time in ten days, using drones to overwhelm positions left without air defenses.</s> <s>Doctors Without Borders reported a hundred and twenty-three wounded civilians reached Chad by Monday — and that's only those who made it across.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>An Israeli airstrike killed two people in Beddawi refugee camp in northern Lebanon.</s> <s>Lebanon's military has cordoned Palestinian camps under a weapons agreement with the Palestinian Authority, leaving two hundred and fifty thousand refugees confined and unarmed as strikes push further north.</s> <s>Authorities now face an impossible choice — whether to allow evacuation or risk the camps emptying permanently.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Israel acquitted the only soldiers prosecuted for abuse at Sde Teiman detention facility, where Gaza detainees have reported systematic mistreatment.</s> <s>The case centered on footage showing soldiers beating a Palestinian prisoner — footage that prosecutors couldn't turn into a conviction.</s> <s>No further prosecutions are planned, and the military courts retain full control over detainee conditions.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Turkey barred observers from the corruption trial of Istanbul Mayor Ekrem Imamoglu, who broke the ruling party's twenty-five year grip on the city in twenty nineteen.</s> <s>He now faces charges alongside four hundred and six others in what Human Rights Watch calls a political dragnet.</s> <s>A conviction would strip the opposition's most prominent leader of his office just as Turkey approaches its next electoral cycle.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Iran struck Bahrain's desalination plant this month, exposing a vulnerability Gulf states have never had to confront at scale.</s> <s>Over ninety percent of freshwater in the Gulf comes from desalination — there are no rivers, no reservoirs, no backup.</s> <s>Analysts warn that a coordinated attack on Gulf plants would leave millions without drinking water within hours.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Denmark called snap elections, riding a wave of public support after Prime Minister Mette Frederiksen rejected Washington's push to acquire Greenland.</s> <s>The sovereignty standoff has become a national mandate — Frederiksen's approval climbed as she held firm.</s> <s>It'll be Europe's first democratic test of public backlash against American territorial ambitions.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>The Egyptian pound fell to fifty-two against the dollar, and the government isn't intervening.</s> <s>Prime Minister Mostafa Madbuly confirmed the central bank is holding a flexible exchange rate to retain foreign investors, even as fuel costs drive inflation higher.</s> <s>Foreign investors reversed their purchases within hours of re-entering the market, leaving the pound's floor uncertain.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>India's rupee hit a record ninety-four per dollar on Monday as oil prices surged fifty percent this month.</s> <s>India imports eighty-five percent of its oil, and the deepening Iran conflict is rewriting every forecast.</s> <s>Bank of America raised its June target to ninety-four, assuming weeks of fighting... not months.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Cuba's opened talks on property seized sixty-seven years ago — claims worth nine billion dollars with interest held by six thousand American owners.</s> <s>Havana paid six other nations decades ago but never settled with Washington, offering now to negotiate if the US lifts its trade blockade.</s> <s>The government says it simply lacks the reserves to pay without trade revenue — a deadlock older than most of the claimants.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Dengue cases have surged four hundred percent in twenty years, and a new global observatory is now tracking outbreaks across eighty-eight countries in real time.</s> <s>Climate change has expanded the range of the Aedes mosquito until it threatens half the world's population.</s> <s>Health ministries will use the observatory's projections to pre-position treatments before outbreaks peak — if they can move faster than the mosquitoes.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>For decades, the only treatments for sleeping sickness killed up to five percent of the patients they were meant to save.</s> <s>A new oral pill replaces those toxic infusions, bringing care within reach of sixty-five million people at risk across thirty-six countries in central and west Africa.</s> <s>The <sub alias="World Health Organization">WHO</sub>'s twenty thirty elimination target now depends on getting that pill to remote communities, God willing.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Extreme heat in sub-Saharan Africa during early pregnancy measurably reduces male births — confirmed at population scale across a continent for the first time.</s> <s>Male embryos are more vulnerable to heat stress than female ones, a finding with implications far beyond demography.</s> <s>Researchers will next test whether the pattern holds in South Asia, where similar heat extremes are intensifying year on year.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Retaliatory hacking by American companies was illegal until this month.</s> <s>Washington authorized corporate cyber retaliation after concluding it can't defend the private sector against state-sponsored attacks alone.</s> <s>No legal framework governs what happens if a corporate hack-back triggers a response from a foreign government — the escalation ladder doesn't have rungs yet.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Meta confirmed it's ending end-to-end encryption on Instagram direct messages starting May eighth.</s> <s>The change means both Meta and governments will be able to access users' private conversations.</s> <s>SMEX, a West Asian digital rights group, warned this directly endangers activists and journalists across the region who relied on Instagram as a secure channel.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>De Telegraaf, one of the Netherlands' largest newspapers, published an interview with a person who doesn't exist — an AI-generated persona advertising sixteen hundred euro seats on a Dubai evacuation flight that never flew.</s> <s>Flight data confirmed the aircraft never left the ground.</s> <s>The newspaper removed the photo but kept the interview live, raising a question newsrooms haven't had to answer before — what does verification mean when the source itself is synthetic.</s>
</p>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="90%">
<s>That's your briefing from <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news.</s>
</prosody>
</speak>